  "query_preview": "..\nA large and disorganized tropical disturbance is located northeast \nof Saipan and is producing isolated to numerous, locally heavy \nshowers and isolated thunderstorms. This system is expected to move \njust north of the Marianas over the next day. A col remains over the \nCNMI that is keeping winds light. However, a developing monsoonal \nflow into the system is expected to increase the winds beginning \ntonight over all islands. Sustained winds of 15 to 25 mph will be \npossible with gusts of 30 mph. Guam will be more likely to receive \nhigher winds and heavier showers. The unstable airmass and high \nprecipitable water values may allow for heavy showers to develop, \ncreating a potential flooding risk. The monsoon flow is expected to \nbe strongest over Guam but high uncertainty remains in where the \nhighest rainfall amounts will occur and there may be breaks between \ninstances of heavy rainfall. By Friday, dryer, more stable air will \nbring a short period of just isolated showers. Another trough is \nlikely to move into the region over the weekend bringing more \nscattered showers and isolated thunderstorms. Periods of isolated to \nscattered showers are expected to continue early next week.",
